From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SYNTH_VERILOG_SURGERY: edit copies of the sources before
 synthesis
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

SYNTH_VERILOG_SURGERY names a script that copies VERILOG_FILES and
edits the copies before synthesis reads them, so vendored RTL stays as
upstream has it and the changes OpenROAD or a PDK needs live in one
script next to the design's config.mk. It runs as the RTL is read
(canonicalization, memory extraction, the SYNTH_USE_SYN frontend), with
SYNTH_VERILOG_SURGERY_ARGS, then `--out-dir $(OBJECTS_DIR)/surgery --`
and the VERILOG_FILES (by PYTHON_EXE when it ends in .py). It writes one
copy per source under the same file name; a failing script, or a copy
it did not write, stops synthesis.

The net diff of The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenROAD-flow-scripts#4649 at
250b2f537b19, not yet merged. Retires at a //:bump onto an ORFS that
carries it.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
